From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: installer lookups work for an account that may only read the keys

Wine's msi opened the machine's Installer keys (UserData\S-1-5-18\
Components, Products, ...) with KEY_ALL_ACCESS for every lookup --
MsiGetComponentPath, MsiProvideQualifiedComponent, the MsiEnum* family --
and gave up when that was refused. Windows' msi reads them read-only: a
standard user's lookups work.

They are refused once SYSTEM has touched the keys in this server's life:
the shared server stamps SYSTEM's descriptor (users read, admins/SYSTEM
all) on a key without one that SYSTEM create_key()s, and Office's
integrator.exe (run by the Click-to-Run service after a Word crash, e.g.
one killed during its sign-in browser) re-registers Office's components
that way. From then on Word could not locate its resource DLLs
(MSO40UIRES.DLL, MSORES.DLL ...) through msi and every start ended in
"Sorry, something went wrong and Word was unable to start. (6)" -- until
the server restarted (descriptors are not saved), which is why only a
sg-wineserver restart cleared it. Found by tracing the server: the same
open_key(access=000f013f) succeeded before the integrator ran and was
ACCESS_DENIED after.

A key that may not be opened for writing is now opened for reading (only
the lookups: the delete paths keep their meaning).

Gate: test/msireadonly-gate.sh (SG_MUTANT_MSI_NO_READ_FALLBACK fails it).
---
--- a/dlls/msi/registry.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/registry.c
@@ -299,6 +299,26 @@
     return ret;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: the lookups (MsiGetComponentPath, MsiProvideQualifiedComponent,
+ * MsiEnum*, ...) asked for KEY_ALL_ACCESS on the machine's Installer keys and
+ * failed for anyone who may only read them -- as a standard user may on
+ * Windows, where msi reads them read-only. Office's resources are found
+ * through them: once SYSTEM's integrator had re-registered Office (giving the
+ * keys SYSTEM's descriptor), every Word start failed with "(6)". A key that
+ * may not be opened for writing is opened for reading. */
+static LONG msi_reg_open_key( HKEY root, const WCHAR *path, DWORD options, REGSAM access, HKEY *key )
+{
+    LONG res = RegOpenKeyExW( root, path, options, access, key );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MSI_NO_READ_FALLBACK
+    if (res == ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED && (access & ~(KEY_WOW64_64KEY | KEY_WOW64_32KEY)) != KEY_READ)
+    {
+        TRACE( "%s: access denied for %#lx, reading only\n", debugstr_w(path), access );
+        res = RegOpenKeyExW( root, path, options, (access & (KEY_WOW64_64KEY | KEY_WOW64_32KEY)) | KEY_READ, key );
+    }
+#endif
+    return res;
+}
